@startuml periodic-refresh
!pragma layout smetana
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam shadowing false
title Periodic Refresh Task: Maintained at Activity Boundaries

state "No periodic task\nperiodicRefreshTask = nil" as Stopped
state "The connection's single periodic task" as Active {
  state "Wait 20 s\nweak reference to the service" as Sleeping
  state "Check liveness, cancellation, connection" as Check
  state "await synchronizeNow()\nreuses the shared execution task" as Syncing
  [*] --> Sleeping
  Sleeping --> Check : wait finished
  Check --> Syncing : enabled && connected\nsame connectionID and not cancelled
  Syncing --> Sleeping : same connection and next round not cancelled
}

[*] --> Stopped
Stopped --> Active : updatePeriodicRefreshTask(isPlaying:)\n[enabled && connected && (foreground || isPlaying)]
Active --> Stopped : condition no longer holds → cancel + nil
Active --> Stopped : disable / replaced connection / folder lost / deinit
Check --> Stopped : cancelled / service released / stale connection
Syncing --> Stopped : connection replaced or task cancelled while waiting

note right of Stopped
  Maintained from:
  · activateConnection: after activation, before the first sync
  · setForeground: maintain first, then sync immediately
  · $isPlaying.removeDuplicates: uses the event value

  Paused in the foreground: periodic refresh still needed.
  Playing in the background: periodic refresh still needed.
  Paused in the background: periodic refresh stops.
  Condition still holds and a task exists: kept, not re-created.
end note
note right of Active
  Each round is the 20 s wait plus this round's sync time.
  It does not start a concurrent transaction every 20 s.
  Stopping the periodic task does not cancel a shared sync already running.
  An old connection's task waking late cannot act on a new connection.
  No schedule is guaranteed while iOS suspends the app.
end note
@enduml
